                <h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:800;color:var(--md-heading);margin:0 0 14px;">Quick answer</h2>
                <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--md-body);margin:0;">A <strong>food delivery app like Swiggy / Zomato</strong> costs <strong>&#8377;8L&ndash;&#8377;15L ($9.6K&ndash;$18K)</strong> for an MVP in one city, <strong>&#8377;25L&ndash;&#8377;50L ($30K&ndash;$60K)</strong> for the full 4-app suite (Customer + Restaurant + Delivery Partner + Admin), and <strong>&#8377;75L&ndash;&#8377;2Cr+ ($90K&ndash;$240K+)</strong> for multi-city enterprise scale. Below: full breakdown by tier, what drives cost, what you can skip, and what you absolutely cannot skip.</p>
