<section class="md-sec">
        <div class="container">
            <div style="max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid var(--md-border);padding:36px 40px;box-shadow:var(--md-card-shadow);">
                <h2 style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--md-heading);margin:0 0 18px;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">MVP &mdash; &#8377;8L&ndash;&#8377;15L ($9.6K&ndash;$18K)</h2>
                <p>The MVP is the cheapest path to validate the model in one city. <strong>Customer app + admin + basic delivery partner app</strong>, single-platform (typically Android first for India), 10&ndash;14 weeks.</p><h4>What's included:</h4><ul><li>Customer iOS or Android app (single platform) with order flow, payments, basic tracking</li><li>Basic admin dashboard for restaurant onboarding, order management, reports</li><li>Basic delivery partner app with order accept + delivery flow + COD</li><li>Payment integration with 1&ndash;2 gateways (Razorpay + COD typical)</li><li>Maps + ETA (Google Maps SDK), live tracking via WebSocket</li></ul><h4>What's NOT included (you'll add in Phase 2):</h4><ul><li>Restaurant-side app (admin manages menus + availability instead)</li><li>Surge pricing engine</li><li>Loyalty / wallet / referrals</li><li>Multi-city geo-zoning</li><li>Advanced fraud detection</li></ul><p><strong>Honest reality:</strong> The MVP is enough to test product-market fit in 1 city with 20&ndash;50 restaurants. Beyond ~2,000 daily orders, you'll need to upgrade.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
<section class="md-sec alt">
        <div class="container">
            <div style="max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid var(--md-border);padding:36px 40px;box-shadow:var(--md-card-shadow);">
                <h2 style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--md-heading);margin:0 0 18px;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">Growth-tier 4-app suite &mdash; &#8377;25L&ndash;&#8377;50L ($30K&ndash;$60K)</h2>
                <p>The sweet spot for most well-funded food delivery startups. Full 4-app productised suite, 14&ndash;22 weeks.</p><h4>What's included:</h4><ul><li><strong>Customer app</strong> (iOS + Android): full feature set with loyalty, referrals, wallet, multiple addresses, repeat-order</li><li><strong>Restaurant / Vendor app</strong>: menu management, availability, KOT integration, payouts, analytics</li><li><strong>Delivery Partner app</strong>: route optimisation, batch deliveries, SOS, earnings, ratings</li><li><strong>Admin dashboard</strong>: operations, vendor onboarding, finance, surge, analytics, fraud</li><li>Multi-payment Indian stack (UPI, cards, COD, wallets, BNPL)</li><li>Surge + slot pricing engine</li><li>Loyalty + referrals + wallet</li><li>Push notifications + WhatsApp Business API + SMS</li><li>Basic analytics dashboard for unit economics</li></ul><p><strong>When to pick this:</strong> Series A funded, planning to scale to 3&ndash;5 cities in 12 months, want to compete on operational maturity.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
<section class="md-sec">
        <div class="container">
            <div style="max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid var(--md-border);padding:36px 40px;box-shadow:var(--md-card-shadow);">
                <h2 style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--md-heading);margin:0 0 18px;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">Enterprise multi-city &mdash; &#8377;75L&ndash;&#8377;2Cr+ ($90K&ndash;$240K+)</h2>
                <p>For Series B+ operators planning 10+ cities or replacing existing first-party tech.</p><h4>What's added on top of Growth:</h4><ul><li>Multi-city operations module with city-manager dashboards</li><li>Cuisine intelligence + AI-based recommendations</li><li>Advanced fleet management (route optimisation across hubs, dispatch ML)</li><li>Restaurant POS integration (Petpooja, Zomato Order Manager) at scale</li><li>Advanced fraud detection (refund fraud, double-order, fake addresses)</li><li>SOC 2 Type II readiness for enterprise data handling</li><li>BI + analytics layer (BigQuery / Snowflake)</li><li>Multi-region deployment for low-latency in 10+ cities</li></ul><p><strong>Honest reality:</strong> Beyond &#8377;75L, you're effectively rebuilding what Swiggy / Zomato built over 8 years. You can do it; just be honest about what you're committing to.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
<section class="md-sec alt">
        <div class="container">
            <div style="max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid var(--md-border);padding:36px 40px;box-shadow:var(--md-card-shadow);">
                <h2 style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--md-heading);margin:0 0 18px;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">What drives the cost?</h2>
                <p>Five main cost drivers, in order of magnitude:</p><ol><li><strong>Number of apps</strong>: 1 app vs 4 apps is the biggest jump. Each additional app adds 25&ndash;30% of build cost.</li><li><strong>Multi-platform</strong>: iOS + Android is ~50% more than single platform. Cross-platform (Flutter / React Native) reduces this to ~25%.</li><li><strong>Integration depth</strong>: POS (Petpooja), payment gateways, OTAs, marketing tools &mdash; each integration is &#8377;1&ndash;5L of work.</li><li><strong>Compliance + security</strong>: FSSAI display, age + ID verification, SOC 2, GST. Adds &#8377;5&ndash;15L depending on depth.</li><li><strong>Operational complexity</strong>: Surge, multi-city, dark stores, fleet, fraud &mdash; each adds &#8377;5&ndash;30L.</li></ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
<section class="md-sec">
        <div class="container">
            <div style="max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid var(--md-border);padding:36px 40px;box-shadow:var(--md-card-shadow);">
                <h2 style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--md-heading);margin:0 0 18px;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">What you can skip in MVP (and what you can't)</h2>
                <h4>Safe to skip in MVP:</h4><ul><li>Restaurant-side app (admin handles menus)</li><li>iOS app (Android-first for India is fine)</li><li>Surge pricing (flat pricing OK to start)</li><li>Loyalty + referrals (manual coupons OK)</li><li>Advanced analytics (basic dashboard fine for 6 months)</li></ul><h4>You CANNOT skip in MVP:</h4><ul><li><strong>Real-time order tracking</strong> &mdash; customers expect it</li><li><strong>UPI + COD</strong> at minimum (India market won't tolerate missing UPI)</li><li><strong>Push notifications</strong> &mdash; can't survive without delivery updates</li><li><strong>FSSAI compliance display</strong> &mdash; legal requirement</li><li><strong>Customer ratings + reviews</strong> &mdash; required for restaurant accountability</li></ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
